2026-10-26 18:23:40,727 - autofit.non_linear.search.runtime - WARNING - The non-linear search is using multiprocessing (number_of_cores>1), but the following environment variables are not all set to 1: OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS, MKL_NUM_THREADS, OMP_NUM_THREADS, VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS, NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS.

This can lead to performance issues, because both the non-linear search and libraries that may be used in your `log_likelihood_function` evaluation (e.g. NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn) may attempt to parallelize over all cores available, overallocating tasks over the CPUs.

To mitigate this, set the environment variables to 1 in your terminal, so only the non-linear search is parallelized over multiple cores:

    export OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1
    export MKL_NUM_THREADS=1
    export OMP_NUM_THREADS=1
    export VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1
    export NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=1

If you "know what you are doing" and do not want these environment variables to be set to one, disable this warning in the config files: `config -> general.yaml -> parallel: -> warn_environment_variables=False`
